reports/

# Regenerated by `next dev` / `next build` / `next typegen`; the route-type
# import target flips between .next/dev/types and .next/types depending on
# which command last ran, so tracking it creates unrelated working-tree
# churn. Per Next.js's own docs: gitignore it and stop tracking it.
next-env.d.ts
